1
00:04:30,286 --> 00:04:32,579
- Whoo!

2
00:04:58,189 --> 00:05:03,527
You know, showboating like that
just makes you look desperate.

3
00:05:03,611 --> 00:05:07,322
Yeah, "Look at me. I can flip my ski."
Pathetic.

4
00:05:07,406 --> 00:05:10,492
- Yeah.
- Daniel, that was awesome!

5
00:05:11,536 --> 00:05:13,787
- Nicole.

6
00:05:17,583 --> 00:05:19,709
Hey, Daniel, Nicole left, huh?

7
00:05:19,794 --> 00:05:22,879
- Should've let me talk to her.

8
00:05:28,719 --> 00:05:30,554
Whoo-hoo!

9
00:05:37,687 --> 00:05:39,187
I love it out here.

10
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:46,153
The Big Dipper.
It's my favorite.

11
00:05:48,156 --> 00:05:49,823
- Do you know that one?
- No.

12
00:05:49,907 --> 00:05:52,617
- I got a D in Astronomy.

13
00:05:56,747 --> 00:05:59,624
So, I never see you with anyone.

14
00:05:59,709 --> 00:06:03,086
Do you have a girlfriend
out of town or something?

15
00:06:10,094 --> 00:06:12,179
Daniel? Daniel?

16
00:06:18,936 --> 00:06:22,105
I want you to feel this!

17
00:06:23,482 --> 00:06:26,860
This is what's coming for you.

18
00:06:30,072 --> 00:06:31,198
Daniel, are you Ok?

19
00:06:33,409 --> 00:06:34,993
Oh, my God.

20
00:06:39,832 --> 00:06:43,001
He's a freak.
He's some kind of freak.

21
00:07:28,798 --> 00:07:30,006
Number Three's dead.

22
00:07:31,634 --> 00:07:34,010
- You all right?

23
00:07:35,096 --> 00:07:37,889
- Yeah.
- Anyone else see what happened?

24
00:08:18,556 --> 00:08:22,434
I told you not to keep this
crap. It just slows us down.

25
00:08:49,337 --> 00:08:51,046
All right, let's go.

26
00:08:58,554 --> 00:09:00,013
Daniel.

27
00:09:07,188 --> 00:09:10,940
This is the part
I hate the most, the running.

28
00:09:11,025 --> 00:09:14,235
But it's the only thing
in my life that's real.

29
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,112
The rest is a lie.

30
00:09:16,197 --> 00:09:18,365
Even Henri.

31
00:09:18,449 --> 00:09:20,325
People think he's my father.

32
00:09:20,409 --> 00:09:21,993
He's not.

33
00:09:22,078 --> 00:09:26,581
He's a warrior from my planet,
assigned to keep me alive.

34
00:09:27,917 --> 00:09:30,126
I don't remember my father.

35
00:09:30,211 --> 00:09:33,338
All he left for me was
some kind of box.

36
00:09:33,422 --> 00:09:36,132
Henri says he'll pass it on
to me when the time is right.

37
00:09:38,886 --> 00:09:41,930
I got my first scar when
I was nine years old,

38
00:09:42,014 --> 00:09:44,516
near the border of Mexico.

39
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:47,352
It woke me from my sleep.

40
00:09:47,436 --> 00:09:51,439
It was the first sign that the
Mogadorians had found us here on Earth.

41
00:09:52,274 --> 00:09:55,193
The second scar
came when I was 12.

42
00:09:55,277 --> 00:09:58,571
I was in Colorado, in the
middle of a spelling bee.

43
00:09:59,573 --> 00:10:02,784
As soon as I felt it, I
knew Number Two was dead.

44
00:10:04,036 --> 00:10:06,788
Last night, I got my third scar.

45
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:14,379
I was just a kid when the Mogadorians
invaded my planet, Lorien.

46
00:10:14,463 --> 00:10:16,881
Nine of us children escaped.

47
00:10:16,966 --> 00:10:21,386
We were gifted, meant to protect
our people when we grew up.

48
00:10:21,470 --> 00:10:25,140
We never got the chance.
Everyone was killed.

49
00:10:26,392 --> 00:10:29,227
We are the last of our kind.

50
00:10:29,311 --> 00:10:33,523
Three of us are gone. Dead.

51
00:10:33,607 --> 00:10:36,818
They are hunting us down,
one by one, in order.

52
00:10:38,654 --> 00:10:40,405
I know I'm next.

53
00:10:42,199 --> 00:10:43,575
I am Number Four.

54
00:10:43,659 --> 00:10:44,951
All right, well, so...

55
00:10:45,035 --> 00:10:47,912
Daniel won't be in school
the rest of the semester.

56
00:10:47,997 --> 00:10:50,457
Ok. You, too.

57
00:10:52,501 --> 00:10:53,835
Your new ID.

58
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:59,090
And this time, you stay out of sight,
huh? No school, no teams, nothing.

59
00:10:59,175 --> 00:11:01,134
John Smith. Very original.

60
00:11:01,218 --> 00:11:04,345
I don't want to be original.
I want to be invisible.

61
00:11:08,225 --> 00:11:10,351
This time was different.

62
00:11:10,436 --> 00:11:12,395
I didn't just get a scar.

63
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:15,023
I, uh... I saw Number Three.

64
00:11:17,151 --> 00:11:20,778
I felt the knife, I felt him
die. I could tell we all did.

65
00:11:22,031 --> 00:11:25,366
- The others.
- We should get moving.

66
00:11:25,451 --> 00:11:28,077
Mogadorians could've already
picked up our scent.

67
00:11:29,413 --> 00:11:32,874
We're going to Paradise. I
have business to take care of.

68
00:12:41,944 --> 00:12:43,027
It's Bernie Kosar.

69
00:12:45,030 --> 00:12:46,447
Played football.

70
00:12:50,202 --> 00:12:54,330
- Yeah, he played for Cleveland.
- Hm. Good to know.

71
00:12:54,415 --> 00:12:57,125
- Next time, I get to pick the place.
- Yeah.

72
00:13:28,991 --> 00:13:31,618
That's all of it.
I'm going to bed.

73
00:13:31,702 --> 00:13:35,288
Ooh. Hang on. I
need a new picture.

74
00:13:36,624 --> 00:13:39,083
We have to wipe out anything
that hits the Internet.

75
00:13:39,168 --> 00:13:42,462
- Say "Paradise."

76
00:13:48,552 --> 00:13:49,552
Oh, shit.

77
00:13:49,637 --> 00:13:51,804
This is why
I need you to be invisible.

78
00:14:23,379 --> 00:14:24,379
Get back inside.

79
00:14:26,340 --> 00:14:27,674
John.

80
00:14:27,758 --> 00:14:31,260
Come on. Come back inside.

81
00:14:40,854 --> 00:14:43,981
Little small for a
Mogadorian, don't you think?

82
00:14:46,402 --> 00:14:48,194
I'm sure he belongs to someone.

83
00:14:48,278 --> 00:14:51,364
He doesn't
have any collar or tags.

84
00:14:51,448 --> 00:14:53,991
Hm. Somebody, somewhere,
must miss you, huh?

85
00:14:57,037 --> 00:14:58,413
- Come on.

86
00:14:58,497 --> 00:15:01,165
Another pair of eyes and
ears watching the house?

87
00:15:01,917 --> 00:15:05,211
- I'm gonna need somebody to talk to.
-  Talk to me.

88
00:15:07,631 --> 00:15:09,507
Yeah, keep the dog.

89
00:15:09,591 --> 00:15:10,967
What are you gonna call him?

90
00:15:12,428 --> 00:15:15,304
- How about Bernie Kosar?

91
00:16:52,569 --> 00:16:54,278
What are you doing up?

92
00:16:54,363 --> 00:16:55,947
- I changed my mind.

93
00:16:56,031 --> 00:16:57,865
About what?

94
00:16:57,950 --> 00:17:00,910
Look, uh, as much fun as
you are to be around,

95
00:17:00,994 --> 00:17:04,080
I can't be a prisoner. Uh,
I have to go to school.

96
00:17:04,164 --> 00:17:06,165
- No. No way, too risky.
- Come on.

97
00:17:06,250 --> 00:17:08,751
Number Three was completely off
the grid and the Mogs got him.

98
00:17:08,836 --> 00:17:10,336
- Didn't save him.
- Mm-mm.

99
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:13,965
Come on. I'm gonna be
safer if I blend in.

100
00:17:14,049 --> 00:17:15,508
I promise I'll keep
a low profile.

101
00:17:15,592 --> 00:17:17,718
Look. Even if I let
you, and I'm not,

102
00:17:17,803 --> 00:17:20,012
you can't just waltz into
school and start class...

103
00:17:20,097 --> 00:17:22,682
Do you think you're the only
one who can forge documents?

104
00:17:23,976 --> 00:17:26,394
Hm. Do you have a...?

105
00:17:26,478 --> 00:17:29,063
Five days of rations,
spare clothes, GPS, cash.

106
00:17:30,566 --> 00:17:31,846
- What's your name?
- John Smith.

107
00:17:31,859 --> 00:17:33,359
- Where are you from?
- Toronto.

108
00:17:33,443 --> 00:17:35,319
You seem kind of
tan for Toronto.

109
00:17:35,404 --> 00:17:39,574
Santa Fe, New Mexico.
I know the drill, Ok?

110
00:17:43,756 --> 00:17:45,597
You keep this on you.
I'll call you every hour.

111
00:17:45,622 --> 00:17:47,206
If you don't pick up, I
know something's wrong.

112
00:17:47,291 --> 00:17:50,459
- Come on, every hour?
- That, or you can home school.

113
00:17:50,544 --> 00:17:52,545
And I'll be your teacher.

114
00:17:53,714 --> 00:17:55,047
Fine.

115
00:17:55,132 --> 00:17:59,010
Hey, John, don't be stupid.
You keep your head down.

116
00:17:59,094 --> 00:18:00,136
I know how to blend in.

117
00:18:23,201 --> 00:18:24,535
Ok, doll. Take a seat.

118
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:27,038
I'll just print up your
schedule. Back in a jiffy.

119
00:18:30,959 --> 00:18:32,560
I know she's
the star photographer,

120
00:18:32,628 --> 00:18:34,462
but it's not fair to
the other students.

121
00:18:34,546 --> 00:18:36,172
She's using up all
the vital supplies.

122
00:18:36,256 --> 00:18:40,051
Emory, come on. "Strangers in
Paradise." At least she's creative.

123
00:18:40,135 --> 00:18:42,637
The pictures on her website
are totally inappropriate.

124
00:18:42,721 --> 00:18:46,182
Mr. Behrman, if you want to keep
the photos, you should just say so.

125
00:18:46,266 --> 00:18:48,643
Keep the photos? They're
already all over the Internet!

126
00:18:48,727 --> 00:18:52,063
It's a violation to post things like
this without people's permission.

127
00:18:52,147 --> 00:18:53,439
You have to do
something about this.

128
00:18:53,523 --> 00:18:55,942
Mr. Behrman,
excuse us for a few minutes, Ok?

129
00:19:03,533 --> 00:19:06,911
Sarah, this is not like you.

130
00:19:06,995 --> 00:19:09,372
Is there something going on?

131
00:19:09,456 --> 00:19:12,333
- Everything's fine.
- Sarah?

132
00:19:12,417 --> 00:19:15,378
- Honestly.
- Have a seat.

133
00:19:16,296 --> 00:19:19,548
You can't let a few negative
students get you down.

134
00:19:19,633 --> 00:19:23,386
Look, I don't want you to isolate
yourself from the rest of the school.

135
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:28,474
- You should enjoy this year.
- Ok, I'll try.

136
00:19:28,558 --> 00:19:31,644
- Good.
- Can I please have my camera back?

137
00:19:31,728 --> 00:19:35,356
No more photos on your website without
teacher and student permission.

138
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:37,108
OK.

139
00:19:37,192 --> 00:19:38,859
Here's your schedule.

140
00:19:42,406 --> 00:19:46,117
Homeroom is calculus. That's
B-wing, room seven...

141
00:19:46,201 --> 00:19:51,956
Oh, Sarah! Could you show our friend
to his locker? He's from Santa Fe.

142
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:56,502
Job fair starts tomorrow.
Everybody, job fair starts tomorrow.

143
00:19:56,586 --> 00:19:59,672
- What kind of camera do you use?

144
00:20:00,590 --> 00:20:02,925
Eavesdropping? That's not
gonna win you friends.

145
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:04,593
- Check it out.
- What?

146
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:08,764
Tell that to the principal with
a fish tank for an office.

147
00:20:09,516 --> 00:20:12,018
It's kind of hard not to hear.

148
00:20:13,353 --> 00:20:17,523
Sorry. This whole place
is kind of a fish tank.

149
00:20:18,525 --> 00:20:20,985
Well... Room seven
is down the hall,

150
00:20:21,069 --> 00:20:23,654
and, uh, that's your
locker right there.

151
00:20:25,615 --> 00:20:28,743
Good luck... um...

152
00:20:28,827 --> 00:20:30,578
Oh, uh, John...

153
00:20:30,662 --> 00:20:32,747
Smith.

154
00:20:34,541 --> 00:20:37,793
Ok. You don't want to
tell me your name.

155
00:20:37,878 --> 00:20:38,878
That's fine.

156
00:20:45,802 --> 00:20:49,221
That's really my name.
John Smith.

157
00:20:58,482 --> 00:21:00,941
What's up, man? You new?

158
00:21:02,611 --> 00:21:06,906
Mark James. This is Kevin,
Jackson, Tyler and Max.

159
00:21:06,990 --> 00:21:08,699
-  Hey, man, what's up?
- John.

160
00:21:08,784 --> 00:21:10,701
Good to meet you, John.
Where are you from?

161
00:21:10,786 --> 00:21:13,704
- Santa Fe.
- Oh, New Mexico.

162
00:21:13,789 --> 00:21:15,081
Play any ball out there?

163
00:21:15,165 --> 00:21:17,708
- Football?
- Yeah.

164
00:21:17,793 --> 00:21:20,336
- No.
- Play anything?

165
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:22,546
Baseball? Soccer? Ping-pong?

166
00:21:22,631 --> 00:21:25,049
- Nope.

167
00:21:25,133 --> 00:21:28,677
Ok. No, that's cool, man.
That's totally cool.

168
00:21:28,762 --> 00:21:30,679
We could always use more
boosters in the stands, right?

169
00:21:30,764 --> 00:21:35,017
Listen. You need anything,
you ask us, Ok?

170
00:21:35,102 --> 00:21:38,104
- We got you.
- I'll keep that in mind.

171
00:21:38,188 --> 00:21:42,650
- Good talking to you, big guy.

172
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,693
- Look who it is.

173
00:21:44,778 --> 00:21:46,946
- Watch out, man.

174
00:21:47,030 --> 00:21:48,614
Sorry, Sam.

175
00:21:48,698 --> 00:21:52,618
-  Loser!

176
00:21:55,122 --> 00:21:56,288
Wait up, fool.

177
00:21:56,373 --> 00:21:57,623
Thanks.

178
00:21:59,417 --> 00:22:00,918
Gotta love the classics.

179
00:22:01,002 --> 00:22:03,838
Homecoming King versus
the science nerd.

180
00:22:05,423 --> 00:22:07,883
Just get better with
time, don't they?

181
00:22:07,968 --> 00:22:11,428
- That guy, Mark, he's...
- Soon to be irrelevant.

182
00:22:11,513 --> 00:22:13,973
He's in the third year of the
best four years of his life.

183
00:23:16,620 --> 00:23:20,706
So, she was like, "The solar system's
sun does not revolve around the Earth."

184
00:23:20,790 --> 00:23:22,708
I said, "Yeah, right."

185
00:23:25,670 --> 00:23:27,004
-  Hey, Spock!

186
00:23:27,088 --> 00:23:29,840
- Nailed it!
- Heads up! UFO, brother!

187
00:23:29,925 --> 00:23:32,218
- That had to hurt.

188
00:23:32,302 --> 00:23:34,011
Hey, stay down, man.
Just stay down.

189
00:23:34,095 --> 00:23:35,335
He's gonna cry. He's gonna cry.

190
00:23:35,347 --> 00:23:37,765
- Oh, Mommy's coming!
-  Oh...

191
00:23:40,143 --> 00:23:42,394
-  Right in the face.
- Hey, are you Ok?

192
00:23:42,479 --> 00:23:46,357
- Assholes.
- Yo, new dude! Little help?

193
00:23:56,243 --> 00:23:58,118
Jesus!

194
00:23:58,203 --> 00:24:00,246
I'm fine! Get off me.

195
00:24:00,330 --> 00:24:02,122
Come on, man!

196
00:24:02,207 --> 00:24:04,166
- You Ok?
-  No.

197
00:24:08,004 --> 00:24:10,589
That's quite an arm
you got there.

198
00:24:10,674 --> 00:24:13,467
Yeah. Who knew?

199
00:24:15,512 --> 00:24:17,846
So, uh, what's with
the UFO thing?

200
00:24:19,641 --> 00:24:21,041
I know it's your
first day and all,

201
00:24:21,059 --> 00:24:23,644
but, uh, sooner or later
you'll figure it out.

202
00:24:24,729 --> 00:24:25,813
Figure what out?

203
00:24:27,023 --> 00:24:29,441
I'm definitely not the guy
you want to hang with.

204
00:25:25,248 --> 00:25:27,291
Invisible.

205
00:25:27,375 --> 00:25:29,293
You heard me when I
said that, right?

206
00:25:29,377 --> 00:25:33,422
Yeah. Yeah, because I
remember you being there.

207
00:26:18,468 --> 00:26:22,346
Let us face,
without panic, the reality of our times.

208
00:26:22,430 --> 00:26:24,264
- The fact that atom bombs

209
00:26:24,349 --> 00:26:28,519
may, some day, be dropped on our cities.
And let us prepare for survival

210
00:26:28,603 --> 00:26:30,604
by understanding the
weapon that threatens us.

211
00:26:30,688 --> 00:26:31,688
Yeah.

212
00:26:37,946 --> 00:26:41,407
- How you settling in, bro?

213
00:26:42,659 --> 00:26:45,702
- Fine, thanks.
- Good. That's good.

214
00:26:45,787 --> 00:26:49,123
- I see you and Spock are vibing.

215
00:26:49,207 --> 00:26:51,125
Got a bit of a soft spot
for freaks, do you?

216
00:26:51,209 --> 00:26:52,918
Who's talking?

217
00:26:54,963 --> 00:26:57,923
Yikes.

218
00:26:58,007 --> 00:27:01,969
Look. It's cute, it really is.
You are an adorable young man.

219
00:27:02,053 --> 00:27:04,221
But I find it irritating,

220
00:27:04,305 --> 00:27:06,432
so keep it on the bleachers, Ok?

221
00:27:06,516 --> 00:27:08,600
- All right.
- Good. That's good.

222
00:27:08,685 --> 00:27:10,310
Also, while I'm here,

223
00:27:10,395 --> 00:27:11,979
I'm gonna let you
in on a little tip.

224
00:27:27,579 --> 00:27:31,290
Find your place fast. Catch
the rest of this flick, Ok?

225
00:27:31,374 --> 00:27:33,459
Jesus, dude. You
are soaking wet.

226
00:28:02,947 --> 00:28:04,990
John, get up.
Come on. We gotta go.

227
00:28:05,074 --> 00:28:06,074
John.

228
00:28:06,159 --> 00:28:08,660
- John.
- My hands. What...?

229
00:28:08,745 --> 00:28:10,996
- Henri. My hands burn!
- John...

230
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:12,998
- Look at me and relax.
-  What's happening to me?

231
00:28:13,082 --> 00:28:14,625
They called them
legacies back home.

232
00:28:14,709 --> 00:28:17,336
You, the nine, you're the
only ones who have them.

233
00:28:17,420 --> 00:28:18,712
- Legacies?
- That's right.

234
00:28:18,796 --> 00:28:20,797
Your parents were members
of the Lorien Garde.

235
00:28:20,882 --> 00:28:23,342
You've inherited their
abilities. Gifts.

236
00:28:23,426 --> 00:28:24,551
- Gifts?
- That's right.

237
00:28:24,636 --> 00:28:26,386
My hands light up
like road flares.

238
00:28:26,471 --> 00:28:29,014
- And you call that a gift?
- Each legacy has it's own function.

239
00:28:29,098 --> 00:28:31,099
There's... There's
more coming?

240
00:28:31,184 --> 00:28:35,812
As you breathe and focus, you're
gonna learn to control them.

241
00:28:35,897 --> 00:28:39,733
- Ok. Ok.
- Just like you're doing, right now.

242
00:28:39,817 --> 00:28:42,110
- Ok?

243
00:28:43,363 --> 00:28:44,488
How do your hands feel?

244
00:28:45,615 --> 00:28:49,660
-  Better.
- Good.

245
00:28:51,538 --> 00:28:53,038
So, what now?

246
00:28:53,748 --> 00:28:55,249
Now?

247
00:28:55,333 --> 00:28:58,460
We wait. You're gonna keep
growing stronger and faster.

248
00:28:58,545 --> 00:29:00,170
I need you to be careful.

249
00:29:00,255 --> 00:29:03,382
Right now, you have to focus
your mind. Get some control.

250
00:29:03,466 --> 00:29:05,551
When you can do that, you
can get back to school.

251
00:29:05,635 --> 00:29:08,220
I don't want to raise suspicion.
I still have business here.

252
00:29:08,304 --> 00:29:10,097
In the meantime, your powers
will only draw attention.

253
00:29:10,181 --> 00:29:12,474
You keep yourself in
check, you understand?

254
00:29:12,559 --> 00:29:15,102
So I got all these powers, but
I'm not allowed to use them?

255
00:29:15,186 --> 00:29:16,353
Exactly.

256
00:31:16,516 --> 00:31:19,726
- A little early for Thanksgiving.

257
00:31:20,853 --> 00:31:22,354
Paper or plastic?

258
00:31:42,583 --> 00:31:45,335
Whoa.

259
00:32:08,735 --> 00:32:09,818
And you wind it here...

260
00:32:29,672 --> 00:32:31,381
"Strangers in Paradise"?

261
00:32:33,968 --> 00:32:36,511
I know. Arty, pretentious.

262
00:32:36,596 --> 00:32:38,764
Uh... That's not actually
what I was gonna say.

263
00:32:38,848 --> 00:32:42,142
I just needed a name for my
website and it was right there.

264
00:32:44,395 --> 00:32:48,190
You know, they should've
called this town "Ironic."

265
00:32:48,274 --> 00:32:51,276
Ironic, Ohio? Has
a ring to it.

266
00:32:53,988 --> 00:32:57,491
What's up with you? You look
different, or something.

267
00:32:57,575 --> 00:32:59,409
Sarah, come over!
I got a new bike!

268
00:32:59,494 --> 00:33:02,078
-  Ok, I will next week.

269
00:33:02,163 --> 00:33:04,456
- Hold this for a second.
- All right.

270
00:33:04,540 --> 00:33:06,583
- Oh, they're so cute.

271
00:33:06,667 --> 00:33:08,752
You know, uh... I mean it.

272
00:33:08,836 --> 00:33:10,378
Uh... Your photographs...

273
00:33:10,463 --> 00:33:12,923
My parents make me
babysit for film money,

274
00:33:13,007 --> 00:33:17,135
and those are two of my victims.

275
00:33:17,220 --> 00:33:19,596
You know, I'm, uh...

276
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:23,058
I'm actually trying to pay
you a compliment, but, uh...

277
00:33:23,142 --> 00:33:24,518
it's not going so well.

278
00:33:25,645 --> 00:33:27,145
Oh.

279
00:33:27,855 --> 00:33:30,106
Right. Um...

280
00:33:32,276 --> 00:33:33,443
Thank you.

281
00:33:35,404 --> 00:33:38,782
I don't know, I just, um, see
better through this thing.

282
00:33:41,202 --> 00:33:43,745
It's like my own
personal BS detector.

283
00:33:46,082 --> 00:33:47,290
Come on! Let's go!

284
00:33:49,377 --> 00:33:53,296
Excuse me. Did you forget something?
You had two things to do, you know?

285
00:33:53,381 --> 00:33:55,549
- Lock the door and turn off the lights!
-  That's Sam's dad?

286
00:33:55,633 --> 00:33:56,675
His stepdad.

287
00:33:56,759 --> 00:33:59,761
Every night it's the
same thing with you!

288
00:34:05,101 --> 00:34:06,560
This is it.

289
00:34:15,194 --> 00:34:16,403
You live here?

290
00:34:17,697 --> 00:34:20,073
Yeah, I grew up here.

291
00:34:24,579 --> 00:34:28,081
- It's just a house.
- I know.

292
00:34:33,838 --> 00:34:35,005
You hungry?

293
00:34:35,089 --> 00:34:38,383
So, John, just moved from
Santa Fe a few weeks ago.

294
00:34:38,467 --> 00:34:40,051
- The Smiths, right?
- Uh, yes, Sir.

295
00:34:40,136 --> 00:34:43,179
- And your father's a writer?
- Yes, he is.

296
00:34:43,264 --> 00:34:45,932
Everybody really does know
everything in this town.

297
00:34:46,017 --> 00:34:48,518
Oh, gossip spreads like Ebola.

298
00:34:48,603 --> 00:34:49,924
- Question game!

299
00:34:49,937 --> 00:34:52,188
- Oh! Sorry, my bad.

300
00:34:52,273 --> 00:34:54,393
- All right, everybody, surrender them.
- Here you go.

301
00:34:54,442 --> 00:34:57,736
All electronic devices.
Come on, Sarah. Thank you.

302
00:34:57,820 --> 00:34:58,945
Hand them over.

303
00:34:59,030 --> 00:35:00,739
- And you.
-  Mom?

304
00:35:00,823 --> 00:35:03,783
He'll get it back after dinner.
You'll get it back after dinner.

305
00:35:03,868 --> 00:35:06,411
- Thank you, John. See? It's fine.
- All right.

306
00:35:06,495 --> 00:35:10,790
So, Santa Fe's kind of hip,
right? You bored silly here?

307
00:35:10,875 --> 00:35:13,501
Nah, not with the spring
carnival coming up!

308
00:35:13,586 --> 00:35:16,463
It's fun, and you and your
folks should definitely come.

309
00:35:16,547 --> 00:35:18,798
Oh, it's just me and my dad.

310
00:35:19,884 --> 00:35:20,884
Where's your mom?

311
00:35:20,968 --> 00:35:22,510
- Uh... My...
- Mom.

312
00:35:22,595 --> 00:35:27,057
No, it's fine. My dad and mom,
uh, they didn't get married.

313
00:35:27,141 --> 00:35:30,018
Uh, you know, check it out.
Carnival.

314
00:35:30,102 --> 00:35:32,437
Sarah will be there taking
pictures for the paper.

315
00:35:32,521 --> 00:35:33,605
Cheap labor.

316
00:35:33,689 --> 00:35:35,273
-  That is not why.
- No.

317
00:35:35,358 --> 00:35:38,109
- She's a very talented photographer.
-  Question game!

318
00:35:38,194 --> 00:35:41,237
Ok. Keep your voice
down, and we will play.

319
00:35:41,322 --> 00:35:44,991
It's a dinner tradition. Otherwise,
we'd never talk about the good stuff.

320
00:35:45,076 --> 00:35:46,409
Worst advice you ever got?

321
00:35:47,453 --> 00:35:48,703
"Pull this."

322
00:35:48,788 --> 00:35:49,996
-  Oh, stop!

323
00:35:50,081 --> 00:35:51,665
- That's really gross.

324
00:35:51,749 --> 00:35:52,916
Ok, um...

325
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:55,210
"Your parents will never
know you're gone."

326
00:35:55,294 --> 00:35:57,295
It worked with your folks.
That's how she got here.

327
00:35:57,380 --> 00:35:58,838
- Stop it. Stop.
- Oh, my God.

328
00:35:58,923 --> 00:36:00,843
-  What?
-  Ok, Sarah, your turn.

329
00:36:00,883 --> 00:36:05,679
Oh. Mom telling me that self-Tanner
looks totally natural.

330
00:36:05,763 --> 00:36:07,931
- She was orange.

331
00:36:08,015 --> 00:36:10,433
Like a traffic cone.
On picture day.

332
00:36:10,518 --> 00:36:12,018
Oh, you should go
get that picture.

333
00:36:12,103 --> 00:36:13,311
- We still have the picture!
- John, you are gonna...

334
00:36:13,396 --> 00:36:15,105
Why would you want
to show him that?

335
00:36:15,189 --> 00:36:17,440
- I shouldn't have said it.

336
00:36:17,525 --> 00:36:19,609
I think I tore them up.

337
00:36:25,533 --> 00:36:27,367
Sorry about that.

338
00:36:28,577 --> 00:36:32,580
- About what?
- My parents.

339
00:36:32,665 --> 00:36:36,084
They were putting on the
"aren't we cool?" show.

340
00:36:36,168 --> 00:36:37,794
They seem very proud of you.

341
00:36:37,878 --> 00:36:39,796
Yeah, and they're already
trying to convince me

342
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:42,173
to go to the local community
college in Dayton.

343
00:36:42,258 --> 00:36:45,301
They'd love it if I stayed here.

344
00:36:45,386 --> 00:36:48,471
Got into wedding photography.

345
00:36:48,556 --> 00:36:51,516
- What do you want to do?

346
00:36:55,646 --> 00:36:57,439
That's my favorite.

347
00:36:57,523 --> 00:36:59,024
It's got all these light leaks

348
00:36:59,108 --> 00:37:02,152
so the photos come
out so interesting.

349
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:05,030
Here, I'll show you.

350
00:37:14,957 --> 00:37:17,083
See that one right there?

351
00:37:17,168 --> 00:37:19,044
That's what I was talking about.

352
00:37:20,755 --> 00:37:22,422
What's this?

353
00:37:24,258 --> 00:37:25,258
Um...

354
00:37:27,094 --> 00:37:32,265
That is kind of
private, actually.

355
00:37:34,226 --> 00:37:35,935
It's amazing.

356
00:37:41,650 --> 00:37:44,110
- What?
-  You...

357
00:37:45,362 --> 00:37:47,864
You're allowed to look
at everyone else...

358
00:37:47,948 --> 00:37:52,202
take our pictures, but, uh...
we're not allowed to see you?

359
00:37:58,876 --> 00:38:01,044
Ok.
That's enough.

360
00:38:04,173 --> 00:38:06,007
Seems like you want to run away.

361
00:38:06,092 --> 00:38:08,093
I'll just be happy when
I can get out of here.

362
00:38:08,177 --> 00:38:09,886
I don't know. I've been
to a lot of places.

363
00:38:09,970 --> 00:38:12,430
You don't have to give me the
"there's no place like home" speech.

364
00:38:12,515 --> 00:38:14,057
- I've heard it.

365
00:38:14,141 --> 00:38:17,727
No, no. You can go wherever you
want, see whatever you want to.

366
00:38:17,812 --> 00:38:22,148
But a place is only as good
as the people you know in it.

367
00:38:25,069 --> 00:38:26,820
I, uh...

368
00:38:32,535 --> 00:38:35,829
I think this is a
pretty good place.

369
00:38:49,426 --> 00:38:52,345
Bernie, you dumb dog.

370
00:38:54,598 --> 00:38:57,142
- Does he belong to you?
- Yeah. I gotta go.

371
00:38:57,226 --> 00:39:00,770
Well, hey. Hold on a sec.

372
00:39:04,525 --> 00:39:05,733
Um...

373
00:39:10,447 --> 00:39:11,865
Your turn.

374
00:39:16,162 --> 00:39:17,453
Thanks.

375
00:39:32,678 --> 00:39:34,179
I'm fine.

376
00:39:34,263 --> 00:39:36,681
Heard you made quite an
impression in class yesterday.

377
00:39:36,765 --> 00:39:40,018
Flashlight. It was a dumb prank.
But that class...

378
00:39:40,102 --> 00:39:43,104
- Boring as hell? Yeah.
- Yeah.

379
00:39:43,189 --> 00:39:47,317
Look, I know it's none of my business,
but you need to stay off the grid.

380
00:39:47,401 --> 00:39:49,152
- What do you mean?
- It's all over the school.

381
00:39:49,236 --> 00:39:51,571
Mark James and his man-tards
have it out for you.

382
00:39:51,655 --> 00:39:53,656
Sarah may act like one of us...

383
00:39:53,741 --> 00:39:54,866
she's one of them.

384
00:39:54,950 --> 00:39:56,159
He's into Sarah?

385
00:39:56,243 --> 00:39:59,162
More than that. Nobody
can go near her.

386
00:39:59,246 --> 00:40:00,914
- They were like the town...

387
00:40:00,998 --> 00:40:03,291
-  Whoa!

388
00:40:03,375 --> 00:40:04,709
Loser!

389
00:40:04,793 --> 00:40:08,630
No... Ok, come on... Oh, God.

390
00:40:09,506 --> 00:40:11,674
-  Sucks to be you, bro!
-  Seriously.

391
00:40:11,759 --> 00:40:15,303
- Want a napkin? Get a cleanup crew!

392
00:40:17,806 --> 00:40:20,099
I wonder who did that?

393
00:40:22,102 --> 00:40:23,394
What a loser.

394
00:40:23,479 --> 00:40:25,104
Leave me alone!

395
00:40:27,942 --> 00:40:30,026
- Ah, ah, ah...

396
00:40:33,697 --> 00:40:36,324
Did you have a nice
time last night, John?

397
00:40:37,743 --> 00:40:42,205
You see, in football, a
quarterback needs a few things.

398
00:40:42,289 --> 00:40:43,748
Speed, strength...

399
00:40:43,832 --> 00:40:47,502
Mostly, though, you
need intuition.

400
00:40:47,586 --> 00:40:49,921
A feeling when things
are going South.

401
00:40:52,049 --> 00:40:54,968
First time we talked, I
should've listened to mine.

402
00:41:04,311 --> 00:41:07,647
- There you go, John.

403
00:41:09,024 --> 00:41:11,734
- Good boy.

404
00:41:11,819 --> 00:41:14,529
Maybe you got some intuition
working for you, too.

405
00:41:18,284 --> 00:41:19,575
That was awesome.

406
00:41:25,541 --> 00:41:27,375
Raided lost and found.

407
00:41:27,459 --> 00:41:30,169
- Nobody loses anything cool.
- You gotta be kidding me.

408
00:41:30,254 --> 00:41:34,465
Dude, it was that or the Hannah
Montana sweatshirt. You got off easy.

409
00:41:34,550 --> 00:41:37,510
- So, uh...

410
00:41:37,594 --> 00:41:41,180
- ...who's in the picture?
- My dad.

411
00:41:41,265 --> 00:41:43,516
The real one.

412
00:41:54,194 --> 00:41:55,403
Where was that taken?

413
00:41:56,989 --> 00:42:00,283
Mexico. The Yucatán.

414
00:42:00,367 --> 00:42:04,162
We used to go every year looking for
evidence of ancient astronauts.

415
00:42:05,039 --> 00:42:06,581
Ancient astronauts?

416
00:42:06,665 --> 00:42:09,584
Yeah. UFOs and shit.

417
00:42:09,668 --> 00:42:11,711
Freak show stuff.

418
00:42:11,795 --> 00:42:14,422
He called himself an
anthropologist...

419
00:42:14,506 --> 00:42:17,050
He was really just a
foreman at the steel mill.

420
00:42:19,720 --> 00:42:23,181
He spent all his time preparing
for some kind of alien arrival.

421
00:42:25,017 --> 00:42:26,642
I used to think he was a genius.

422
00:42:26,727 --> 00:42:29,604
Had to, I guess.

423
00:42:29,688 --> 00:42:32,190
Nobody wants to admit
their dad's a freak.

424
00:42:47,122 --> 00:42:48,206
Sam...

425
00:42:48,999 --> 00:42:50,333
Sam.

426
00:42:54,254 --> 00:42:55,463
Oh!

427
00:44:43,363 --> 00:44:45,865
Malcolm, what were
you up to here?

428
00:46:05,112 --> 00:46:07,446
Jimmy, Vince,
come on, slow down, boys!

429
00:46:31,138 --> 00:46:32,847
- Hey, Sarah.
- Hey!

430
00:46:46,403 --> 00:46:49,447
Mark James decided to fire
a warning shot about you.

431
00:46:52,534 --> 00:46:56,787
When you first meet somebody, do
you dump all your stuff on them?

432
00:46:56,872 --> 00:46:59,081
All your mistakes, your secrets?

433
00:47:00,208 --> 00:47:04,754
Look, Mark and I, we changed.

434
00:47:04,838 --> 00:47:06,714
I got into photography,

435
00:47:06,798 --> 00:47:11,052
and he wanted me to be his
own personal cheerleader.

436
00:47:11,136 --> 00:47:14,639
Said I was becoming
a total snob.

437
00:47:14,723 --> 00:47:18,100
And when we broke up, that's
what he told everybody.

438
00:47:18,185 --> 00:47:22,188
That I was a total bitch.
And everyone listened.

439
00:47:23,649 --> 00:47:26,275
All my friends.

440
00:47:29,196 --> 00:47:31,739
Uh... I'm sorry.

441
00:47:31,823 --> 00:47:34,950
I'm not. I mean, I was...

442
00:47:35,952 --> 00:47:38,120
but, um, I don't know,

443
00:47:38,205 --> 00:47:41,290
I kinda look at it
like a total gift.

444
00:47:41,375 --> 00:47:43,209
Got away from all of that.

445
00:47:44,628 --> 00:47:49,006
So, uh, what's the hottest
attraction at this place?

446
00:47:55,889 --> 00:47:58,516
You gotta be kidding me, right?
This...

447
00:47:58,600 --> 00:48:00,101
Don't be scared.

448
00:48:20,831 --> 00:48:25,167
-  Save yourself.

449
00:48:42,352 --> 00:48:45,146
Last year, she was
drawn and quartered.

450
00:48:45,230 --> 00:48:47,690
- It was awesome.

451
00:48:50,986 --> 00:48:53,696
-  My God.

452
00:49:04,332 --> 00:49:06,041
Hell's Gate.

453
00:49:06,626 --> 00:49:08,836
Everybody off.

454
00:49:30,150 --> 00:49:31,734
Quite a production.

455
00:49:31,818 --> 00:49:35,780
- Hm. Small town.

456
00:49:48,126 --> 00:49:51,420
Ok. The last part got to me.

457
00:49:53,173 --> 00:49:55,174
- What is that?

458
00:49:56,760 --> 00:49:58,761
- Don't! Let him go! Let him go!

459
00:49:58,845 --> 00:50:01,096
- Stop it!

460
00:50:03,517 --> 00:50:04,517
Hello?

461
00:50:06,686 --> 00:50:08,979
Was that real? Are
you all right?

462
00:50:10,941 --> 00:50:12,942
Let me go! Stop it!

463
00:50:13,026 --> 00:50:14,860
- Leave him alone!

464
00:50:37,008 --> 00:50:38,926
- No!
- Whoa! Calm down.

465
00:50:39,010 --> 00:50:41,971
- Oh, my God. Just get off me!
- Sarah, come here!

466
00:50:42,055 --> 00:50:44,640
- Idiot! It's you!
- Calm down! Calm down!

467
00:50:44,724 --> 00:50:46,976
-  Let go of me.
- You can take off, Ok?

468
00:50:47,060 --> 00:50:49,478
- Let go of me! Let go of me!
- Hey, listen. I will. I will!

469
00:50:50,105 --> 00:50:51,355
Sarah!

470
00:51:05,161 --> 00:51:07,079
Where is she?

471
00:51:07,163 --> 00:51:08,831
It burns, man!

472
00:51:08,915 --> 00:51:12,126
Dude, let go of me, bro, it hurts!

473
00:51:12,210 --> 00:51:15,087
She's at Shepherd Falls! Dude,
put me down. What is that?

474
00:51:20,385 --> 00:51:21,385
Where's John?

475
00:51:21,428 --> 00:51:24,555
I don't get what happened to us.
I don't. I really don't.

476
00:51:24,639 --> 00:51:26,891
So you have your friend
throw me over his shoulder,

477
00:51:26,975 --> 00:51:28,851
drag me through the
woods to come here,

478
00:51:28,935 --> 00:51:32,938
when all you had to do is ask
me! Like a normal person!

479
00:51:33,023 --> 00:51:36,734
You don't have to tell me
I'm being an asshole, Ok?

480
00:51:36,818 --> 00:51:40,029
But you're a problem
for me, Sarah.

481
00:51:40,113 --> 00:51:43,032
Yeah, well, you really
should get over that.

482
00:51:43,116 --> 00:51:46,535
- Wait. Sarah, wait.
- Just stop it!

483
00:51:47,370 --> 00:51:48,954
You Ok?

484
00:52:01,301 --> 00:52:03,636
I hope you can throw
with your left hand.

485
00:52:03,720 --> 00:52:07,973
- No, John, stop! Stop!

486
00:52:19,110 --> 00:52:21,362
John. John, stop. Wait.

487
00:52:21,446 --> 00:52:24,448
Hey. I just didn't want
you to break his arm.

488
00:52:24,532 --> 00:52:26,909
It's not you, it's me. I shouldn't
have lost it like that.

489
00:52:26,993 --> 00:52:28,661
Hey.

490
00:52:31,081 --> 00:52:32,873
Will you walk me home?

491
00:52:41,883 --> 00:52:44,093
You should really
get that looked at.

492
00:52:45,637 --> 00:52:46,929
I will.

493
00:52:48,264 --> 00:52:49,807
I, uh...

494
00:52:55,522 --> 00:52:56,855
I think we should talk.

495
00:53:00,485 --> 00:53:03,445
I know. It's crazy.

496
00:53:04,656 --> 00:53:06,073
Mark is insane.

497
00:53:06,157 --> 00:53:09,034
And this is our last year.

498
00:53:09,119 --> 00:53:11,078
Who knows where you'll
be in three months?

499
00:53:11,162 --> 00:53:13,747
Exactly.

500
00:53:14,708 --> 00:53:16,208
Who knows?

501
00:53:18,378 --> 00:53:21,171
So, I guess I'll just...

502
00:53:21,256 --> 00:53:23,090
see you when I see you?

503
00:53:24,384 --> 00:53:25,592
Yeah.

504
00:53:28,221 --> 00:53:29,555
OK.

505
00:53:36,438 --> 00:53:38,522
Your hand's really warm.

506
00:53:55,123 --> 00:53:57,041
All I think about is you.

507
00:53:57,125 --> 00:53:59,752
All I think about is you, too.

508
00:54:23,693 --> 00:54:25,444
Where did you come from?

509
00:54:27,989 --> 00:54:30,365
All right, Mom! I got it!

510
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:41,085
- I, uh...
- Yeah, I should go.

511
00:54:50,345 --> 00:54:51,345
Bye.

512
00:55:50,321 --> 00:55:53,407
John! In here.

513
00:55:56,369 --> 00:55:57,995
So, what are you?

514
00:56:00,498 --> 00:56:03,709
You threw those football players
around like it was nothing.

515
00:56:03,793 --> 00:56:07,629
And the hand thing?
That's not human.

516
00:56:07,714 --> 00:56:11,008
So I'm asking you, what are you?

517
00:56:13,678 --> 00:56:15,220
Do I need to threaten you?

518
00:56:15,305 --> 00:56:17,639
All right, 'cause I got
some pictures on my phone,

519
00:56:17,724 --> 00:56:19,099
and they're gonna start
some major questions.

520
00:56:19,184 --> 00:56:21,101
- Give me that.
- No.

521
00:56:21,186 --> 00:56:23,478
You know I can hurt you. Hm?

522
00:56:40,038 --> 00:56:42,247
Knock yourself out.

523
00:56:49,422 --> 00:56:52,424
My entire childhood...

524
00:56:53,551 --> 00:56:55,135
has been an episode ofX-Files.

525
00:56:58,181 --> 00:57:00,599
You know what it's like
to feel something...

526
00:57:01,768 --> 00:57:04,519
so strong...

527
00:57:04,604 --> 00:57:06,484
that every day you have
to keep telling yourself

528
00:57:06,564 --> 00:57:09,650
your dad's gonna come back and
take you away from this shithole.

529
00:57:09,734 --> 00:57:12,402
And that everything we
believed in was true.

530
00:57:12,487 --> 00:57:14,947
And that we were not crazy.

531
00:57:19,369 --> 00:57:27,292
Please.

532
00:57:30,922 --> 00:57:32,214
Your dad was right.

533
00:57:34,008 --> 00:57:35,217
What?

534
00:57:41,391 --> 00:57:42,933
He was right.

535
00:57:45,311 --> 00:57:47,479
About ancient astronauts...

536
00:57:48,481 --> 00:57:51,024
life on other planets...

537
00:57:53,361 --> 00:57:54,653
all of it.

538
00:57:59,033 --> 00:58:02,536
Yes! I knew... I knew he
wouldn'tjust leave us!

539
00:58:02,620 --> 00:58:06,540
I mean, they found his truck near the
border of Mexico, and he was just gone.

540
00:58:06,624 --> 00:58:08,417
- Maybe they took him.
- Sam...

541
00:58:08,501 --> 00:58:10,794
If he knew you were
here, he'd come home.

542
00:58:10,878 --> 00:58:14,172
- You can't tell anyone.
- No, I-I-I wouldn't.

543
00:58:14,257 --> 00:58:16,425
No, no, no. You gotta promise
me. Nobody knows this.

544
00:58:16,509 --> 00:58:20,637
There are others from where
I'm from looking for me.

545
00:58:20,722 --> 00:58:23,015
I'm not safe.

546
00:58:23,099 --> 00:58:28,020
Sam! I know you are in there.
Get your ass in the house, now!

547
00:58:29,147 --> 00:58:30,587
Wait until I get
inside and then go.

548
00:58:30,606 --> 00:58:32,316
Sam?

549
00:58:34,360 --> 00:58:35,527
I promise.

550
00:58:38,156 --> 00:58:40,824
-  Yes!

551
00:58:43,911 --> 00:58:45,412
Come on.

552
00:58:59,927 --> 00:59:01,803
Hey, you maniac.

553
00:59:01,888 --> 00:59:05,223
-  Hello, son.
- Hey, what's with the, uh...?

554
00:59:09,729 --> 00:59:10,729
Hello, Dad.

555
00:59:10,772 --> 00:59:12,814
Sheriff James says some
boys got hurt last night.

556
00:59:12,899 --> 00:59:14,941
Couple of them
spent the night in the hospital.

557
00:59:15,026 --> 00:59:16,485
- You said it was four?
- Yeah, four.

558
00:59:16,569 --> 00:59:19,571
- On the football team.
- Yeah, that's right.

559
00:59:19,655 --> 00:59:23,950
Of course, none of them are talking.
That includes my own boy, Mark.

560
00:59:25,703 --> 00:59:29,790
- Your son is Mark?
- Yeah, that's right.

561
00:59:29,874 --> 00:59:31,875
You know, that was his
throwing arm that got hurt.

562
00:59:31,959 --> 00:59:33,919
He said you were there.

563
00:59:36,214 --> 00:59:38,673
Uh, no. I was
actually with a girl.

564
00:59:38,758 --> 00:59:42,803
So I wasn't paying
any attention. Um...

565
00:59:42,887 --> 00:59:43,887
Sarah Hart?

566
00:59:47,600 --> 00:59:52,145
Well, no one wants to be the first
one to say what really happened.

567
00:59:52,230 --> 00:59:55,690
But, eventually, someone will.

568
00:59:55,775 --> 00:59:58,443
I'm sure you're right.
Thank you, Sheriff.

569
00:59:58,528 --> 01:00:00,862
If we hear anything,
we'll let you know.

570
01:00:21,134 --> 01:00:23,760
- Four of them, huh?
- Yeah.

571
01:00:25,388 --> 01:00:27,139
Was it difficult?

572
01:00:28,015 --> 01:00:30,058
Piece of cake.

573
01:00:30,143 --> 01:00:32,727
Good. Means you're getting it.

574
01:00:32,812 --> 01:00:34,813
Go upstairs, pack your stuff.

575
01:00:34,897 --> 01:00:36,231
Because of last night?

576
01:00:36,315 --> 01:00:38,900
Because I don't like people
showing up asking questions.

577
01:00:38,985 --> 01:00:41,987
- And I think this is gonna raise a few.
- "They walk among us."

578
01:00:42,071 --> 01:00:43,947
What is this? Some more
"truth is out there" freaks?

579
01:00:44,031 --> 01:00:46,908
Except that's actually you.

580
01:00:46,993 --> 01:00:49,161
One of the kids must have
caught you on video.

581
01:00:49,245 --> 01:00:50,620
Oh, shit.

582
01:00:50,705 --> 01:00:52,747
He's some kind of freak!

583
01:00:52,832 --> 01:00:54,153
I can't get through
the firewall.

584
01:00:54,167 --> 01:00:55,917
We have to go there and
take it down ourselves.

585
01:00:56,002 --> 01:00:58,128
Mogs see this, just
a matter of time.

586
01:00:58,212 --> 01:01:00,422
Pack your stuff. We're leaving.

587
01:01:01,883 --> 01:01:03,633
I'm not going.

588
01:01:05,011 --> 01:01:06,803
I'm sorry, what did you say?

589
01:01:07,930 --> 01:01:09,556
I'm not going.

590
01:01:09,640 --> 01:01:12,851
Ok. If you want to pick the
next place, that's fine...

591
01:01:12,935 --> 01:01:14,603
It's not my fight
and it never was!

592
01:01:14,687 --> 01:01:16,938
I can't even remember a
world before this one.

593
01:01:17,023 --> 01:01:18,857
Wait, wait...

594
01:01:18,941 --> 01:01:21,234
is this because of a girl?

595
01:01:23,112 --> 01:01:25,071
Go upstairs and get your stuff.

596
01:01:26,282 --> 01:01:29,451
- You're not my father.
- No, no, no. He's dead.

597
01:01:29,535 --> 01:01:32,329
He died for you. In
fact, you know what?

598
01:01:32,413 --> 01:01:36,291
You have no idea how many others have
made sacrifices so you could live!

599
01:01:36,375 --> 01:01:37,876
And it wasn't so you
could come here

600
01:01:37,960 --> 01:01:40,086
and experience puppy love
like a real live boy!

601
01:01:40,171 --> 01:01:41,838
I'm not leaving.

602
01:01:44,675 --> 01:01:47,511
John... John!

603
01:01:47,595 --> 01:01:48,845
- I'm not leaving!

604
01:01:50,139 --> 01:01:53,683
- Oh, yeah, I can do that now.

605
01:01:59,982 --> 01:02:01,107
Hey, John!

606
01:02:12,119 --> 01:02:14,538
I'm letting go, Ok?

607
01:02:15,706 --> 01:02:17,415
- OK?
- OK.

608
01:02:28,427 --> 01:02:31,513
- On our planet...
- Just tell me why they want to kill me.

609
01:02:31,597 --> 01:02:36,059
The Mogs, they don't colonize. They
decimate. And then they move on.

610
01:02:36,143 --> 01:02:38,812
And now, they've moved here.

611
01:02:38,896 --> 01:02:43,775
There are few forces that can stop
them. You and the other five can.

612
01:02:43,859 --> 01:02:45,485
You were saved for
a bigger purpose.

613
01:02:45,570 --> 01:02:49,197
I'm not gonna let you throw
that away for a girl.

614
01:02:49,282 --> 01:02:51,700
She's not just a girl.

615
01:02:54,287 --> 01:02:56,371
I think about leaving her...

616
01:02:57,039 --> 01:02:58,999
but I can't.

617
01:02:59,083 --> 01:03:01,459
And I don't know why.

618
01:03:05,464 --> 01:03:09,342
We don't love like the humans.
With us, it's forever.

619
01:03:13,472 --> 01:03:15,307
You never forget.

620
01:03:17,810 --> 01:03:22,230
If she is that for you,
then don't let them win.

621
01:03:22,315 --> 01:03:24,649
Or you'll never
forgive yourself.

622
01:03:27,778 --> 01:03:28,778
Now, we have to go.

623
01:03:30,114 --> 01:03:32,741
I'll take care of the website
tonight. Buy you a day.

624
01:03:32,825 --> 01:03:36,661
A day? To say goodbye?

625
01:03:36,746 --> 01:03:38,955
That's more than the
rest of us had.

626
01:03:57,475 --> 01:03:59,351
He's some kind of freak!

627
01:04:09,987 --> 01:04:12,656
Henri, I'm going to Sarah's.

628
01:04:16,619 --> 01:04:17,619
Henri?

629
01:04:38,933 --> 01:04:41,685
Henri? Hello? Henri?

630
01:04:41,769 --> 01:04:46,398
No, but come here
and I'll tell you how to find him.

631
01:04:46,482 --> 01:04:48,233
Who are you? Where's Henri?

632
01:04:48,317 --> 01:04:51,194
417 Willard Court,
Warsaw, Indiana.

633
01:05:02,039 --> 01:05:04,290
Come on, come on.

634
01:05:04,375 --> 01:05:05,875
I need your help.

635
01:05:11,090 --> 01:05:12,882
So, you guys...
you guys don't...

636
01:05:12,967 --> 01:05:15,260
- Abduct people?
- Yeah.

637
01:05:15,344 --> 01:05:16,344
No.

638
01:05:16,429 --> 01:05:19,848
But the other guys, the ones
that are chasing you...

639
01:05:19,932 --> 01:05:21,099
they do?

640
01:05:42,496 --> 01:05:43,955
That's it.

641
01:05:45,875 --> 01:05:47,167
Thanks.

642
01:05:54,967 --> 01:05:57,469
Whoa! You brought a gun?

643
01:05:57,553 --> 01:06:00,472
I stole it from Ed. It might
come in handy. Let's go.

644
01:06:00,556 --> 01:06:03,933
- No.
- Dude, I came here to help you.

645
01:06:04,018 --> 01:06:07,520
You have. Now, go home.

646
01:06:25,831 --> 01:06:27,457
- Whoa!

647
01:06:30,211 --> 01:06:32,253
- What are you doing?
- I'm not bailing.

648
01:06:32,338 --> 01:06:34,047
What if these Mog
people took my dad?

649
01:07:06,121 --> 01:07:10,542
-  Holy shit!

650
01:07:10,626 --> 01:07:12,752
But you just dead-bolted it.

651
01:07:14,296 --> 01:07:16,965
- Ok. New plan.
- Yeah.

652
01:07:17,049 --> 01:07:20,134
You follow that guy and you
text me if he comes back, Ok?

653
01:07:20,219 --> 01:07:22,011
Copy that. I'm on it.

654
01:08:56,273 --> 01:08:57,273
Henri.

655
01:09:11,716 --> 01:09:13,557
- Are you Ok?
- You're not supposed to be here.

656
01:09:13,582 --> 01:09:15,708
- What happened?
- The Mogs set this up.

657
01:09:15,793 --> 01:09:18,586
- We need to leave. They're coming.

658
01:09:18,671 --> 01:09:21,589
Everybody stays right where they
are or I'll shoot this kid.

659
01:09:21,674 --> 01:09:24,217
I'll do it! Get your hands up!

660
01:09:24,301 --> 01:09:25,551
So glad you brought the gun.

661
01:09:26,971 --> 01:09:28,262
You're Malcolm's boy.

662
01:09:29,640 --> 01:09:32,850
- Get the lights, will you?
- Shut up! Get your hands up!

663
01:09:38,774 --> 01:09:39,774
Oh!

664
01:09:44,947 --> 01:09:48,449
You! You're the one from
the video on our site.

665
01:09:48,534 --> 01:09:51,577
- The one they're after.
- The one who's after?

666
01:09:51,662 --> 01:09:54,414
- What's he talking about?
- The Mogs, they've been here.

667
01:09:54,498 --> 01:09:55,790
- This was a trap.
-  Yeah.

668
01:09:55,874 --> 01:09:59,293
These dudes, whatever they are, man,
they got plans, know what I'm sayin'?

669
01:09:59,378 --> 01:10:01,629
-  John...
- I'm that guy, the conspiracy guy.

670
01:10:01,714 --> 01:10:04,590
Nobody gives a crap what I say.
But this is real, man!

671
01:10:04,675 --> 01:10:06,050
John. It's time to leave.

672
01:10:06,135 --> 01:10:09,804
They like it here, Earth. They're
gonna take all this shit, everything!

673
01:10:09,888 --> 01:10:11,180
John! Now!

674
01:10:11,265 --> 01:10:13,266
We either do what they say
or we are all gonna die.

675
01:10:13,350 --> 01:10:15,768
- It's time to go! Now!

676
01:10:31,785 --> 01:10:34,871
John. John! John, no!

677
01:11:09,323 --> 01:11:11,157
John, go!

678
01:11:11,241 --> 01:11:12,658
- Now!
- Go!

679
01:11:38,852 --> 01:11:41,354
Start the car. Come on!
Get us out of here!

680
01:11:41,438 --> 01:11:43,158
- I can't find the keys!
- What do you mean?

681
01:11:43,190 --> 01:11:45,650
- I can't find the keys!
- Come on! Come on!

682
01:11:46,527 --> 01:11:48,736
Guys, what are we waiting for?

683
01:11:50,614 --> 01:11:52,490
- I've lost the keys!
- John, start the engine.

684
01:11:52,574 --> 01:11:55,660
- What?
- You can do it. Start the car.

685
01:11:58,497 --> 01:12:00,623
- Come on.
- Start the car.

686
01:12:07,464 --> 01:12:09,632
Whoa, whoa. Come on, come on!
He's coming! He's coming!

687
01:12:09,716 --> 01:12:11,092
- Start the car! Start the car!

688
01:12:11,176 --> 01:12:14,011
Use your magic powers! Come on!
We are so dead!

689
01:12:15,556 --> 01:12:18,099
-  Oh, my God!

690
01:12:22,104 --> 01:12:24,313
- Go! Drive the car!

691
01:12:35,951 --> 01:12:37,618
You take this.

692
01:12:43,000 --> 01:12:45,418
Malcolm was using it
to track the others.

693
01:12:45,502 --> 01:12:48,713
-  Wait. So, my dad was...
- He was helping us.

694
01:12:48,797 --> 01:12:50,965
He was supposed to
bring us together.

695
01:12:52,801 --> 01:12:54,093
You need to find the others.

696
01:12:55,053 --> 01:12:56,554
Together you'll
be more powerful.

697
01:13:09,109 --> 01:13:10,985
I can't do this without you.

698
01:13:13,113 --> 01:13:17,742
Yes, you can.

699
01:13:19,912 --> 01:13:23,831
You have no idea what
you're capable of.

700
01:13:30,088 --> 01:13:31,088
Henri.

701
01:14:27,104 --> 01:14:28,479
Just let me talk.

702
01:14:30,190 --> 01:14:32,817
Ok. So, I called
you like you said.

703
01:14:34,778 --> 01:14:37,113
- I mean, it's not my fault they got...

704
01:14:38,907 --> 01:14:40,866
I mean, we held up our end.

705
01:14:40,951 --> 01:14:43,411
- Hm.
- We're still in?

706
01:14:43,495 --> 01:14:46,789
The whole new world order thing?

707
01:14:46,873 --> 01:14:50,835
The Locator.

708
01:14:50,919 --> 01:14:53,546
- Where is it?
- Ok.

709
01:14:53,630 --> 01:14:57,758
All he had was a
knife and that rock.

710
01:14:59,136 --> 01:15:00,136
And I put it...

711
01:15:02,347 --> 01:15:06,684
- It was over there, man.
- "It was over there, man."

712
01:15:06,768 --> 01:15:08,811
But it's not there now.

713
01:15:31,084 --> 01:15:35,296
Cartoons for children.

714
01:15:35,380 --> 01:15:37,923
Where I'm from,
men have to work.

715
01:15:38,008 --> 01:15:39,842
Look, I'll work hard.

716
01:15:39,926 --> 01:15:43,554
The disregard that so many of
you have for practical matters,

717
01:15:43,638 --> 01:15:48,184
it's... beautiful.

718
01:15:48,268 --> 01:15:50,394
I think we should all
have some fun. Huh?

719
01:15:52,356 --> 01:15:55,399
Gadgets. You call
them "toys for boys."

720
01:15:56,943 --> 01:15:58,694
- I have a gadget.

721
01:15:58,779 --> 01:16:02,615
- Would you like to play with it?
- Uh... No, no. I...

722
01:16:02,699 --> 01:16:07,078
-  It wants to play with you!

723
01:16:20,759 --> 01:16:21,967
Need to talk to you.

724
01:16:22,052 --> 01:16:24,011
Any idea where I might
find your friend?

725
01:16:24,096 --> 01:16:26,680
He's not who you think he is.

726
01:16:26,765 --> 01:16:28,557
Excuse me?

727
01:16:33,705 --> 01:16:35,665
The Paradise Sheriff's Department

728
01:16:35,690 --> 01:16:37,358
raided the home oftwo suspects,

729
01:16:37,442 --> 01:16:40,152
seizing computers and
several suspicious items.

730
01:16:40,237 --> 01:16:43,531
An APB has been issued on the
suspects and anyone with...

731
01:16:47,035 --> 01:16:48,536
We need to get out of here.

732
01:16:50,330 --> 01:16:51,997
There's a news thing.

733
01:16:52,082 --> 01:16:55,209
The cops think you and Henri
are criminals or terrorists.

734
01:17:05,971 --> 01:17:07,555
We're going back.

735
01:17:10,809 --> 01:17:12,726
I'm outside of
the home here in Warsaw

736
01:17:12,811 --> 01:17:15,938
where the mutilated bodies of two
paranormal website operators

737
01:17:16,022 --> 01:17:18,023
were just found a few hours ago.

738
01:17:18,108 --> 01:17:19,859
The police are not saying
if they have any leads

739
01:17:19,943 --> 01:17:22,278
or even why these brutal
murders occurred.

740
01:17:22,362 --> 01:17:24,655
Police have no suspects
at this time...

741
01:17:35,417 --> 01:17:36,876
- I have one of those!
- What?

742
01:17:36,960 --> 01:17:39,670
One of those. I took it
from my dad's stash.

743
01:17:39,754 --> 01:17:41,922
- I need you to get it.
- Yeah, yeah.

744
01:17:42,007 --> 01:17:45,509
Let me off at Linndale.
Sarah's at a house up there.

745
01:17:45,594 --> 01:17:47,511
I'll call you after.

746
01:17:47,596 --> 01:17:49,930
- And then what?
- Then I get the rock and you go home.

747
01:18:00,942 --> 01:18:03,110
- It's him.
- John?

748
01:18:03,737 --> 01:18:07,031
-  Did you see that?
-  What's he doing here?

749
01:18:08,658 --> 01:18:09,742
Yeah, he's here.

750
01:18:14,539 --> 01:18:15,664
That's him!

751
01:18:32,057 --> 01:18:36,352
Come on.

752
01:18:59,292 --> 01:19:01,752
Doesn't seem like
your kind of crowd.

753
01:19:04,714 --> 01:19:07,841
Not so sure who my kind
of crowd is right now.

754
01:19:07,926 --> 01:19:10,469
- Look, just...
- John Smith?

755
01:19:10,554 --> 01:19:12,429
I'm such an idiot.

756
01:19:13,848 --> 01:19:17,059
And they're saying that your
dad is some kind of terrorist.

757
01:19:17,143 --> 01:19:19,270
He's not a terrorist.

758
01:19:19,896 --> 01:19:21,272
Tell me the truth.

759
01:19:22,274 --> 01:19:24,441
- Who are you?

760
01:19:34,953 --> 01:19:36,161
He's upstairs.

761
01:19:37,038 --> 01:19:38,789
All right, guys, out of the way.

762
01:19:40,792 --> 01:19:43,002
You didn't answer my question.

763
01:19:43,920 --> 01:19:45,504
I just came to say goodbye.

764
01:19:45,589 --> 01:19:47,506
- John, wait! What are you... No, John!
- Don't move!

765
01:19:47,591 --> 01:19:49,967
- Sarah!

766
01:19:59,185 --> 01:20:00,185
How...

767
01:20:00,270 --> 01:20:01,687
- Move! Move!
- Go!

768
01:20:17,412 --> 01:20:19,038
That was awesome!

769
01:20:19,122 --> 01:20:22,499
- Whoa...

770
01:20:28,173 --> 01:20:30,049
What you did is not possible.

771
01:20:30,133 --> 01:20:31,634
Who I am...

772
01:20:31,718 --> 01:20:33,677
it's all in here. I
took these for you.

773
01:20:33,762 --> 01:20:37,473
Wait. Come with me. Please.

774
01:20:38,433 --> 01:20:40,768
Any idea where they'd be?

775
01:20:40,852 --> 01:20:43,270
I think I know where
she might go.

776
01:20:53,365 --> 01:20:56,742
- Who the hell are they?
- Big-ass linebackers?

777
01:21:05,085 --> 01:21:07,252
- Holy shit...

778
01:21:11,299 --> 01:21:13,050
- No, no, no!

779
01:21:15,762 --> 01:21:16,845
Dad!

780
01:21:29,359 --> 01:21:33,153
An alcohol-fuelled
young guy like you...

781
01:21:33,238 --> 01:21:37,074
- ...healthy and well-fed.

782
01:21:37,158 --> 01:21:40,744
I bet you watch a lot of television,
don't you? Do you? Do you?

783
01:21:40,829 --> 01:21:42,996
-  Yeah.
- Yeah.

784
01:21:43,081 --> 01:21:45,582
In this situation here,
you're probably thinking,

785
01:21:45,667 --> 01:21:48,836
"Maybe I could save the day.
Maybe I could be the hero."

786
01:21:48,920 --> 01:21:53,132
But I say... don't do that.

787
01:21:53,216 --> 01:21:54,883
OK?

788
01:21:56,594 --> 01:21:59,471
Tell me now, where is the boy?

789
01:22:27,417 --> 01:22:29,918
These are beautiful.

790
01:22:44,559 --> 01:22:46,059
Can you show me?

791
01:23:13,922 --> 01:23:16,256
-  No!
- Get in!

792
01:23:20,512 --> 01:23:23,972
Let me go! Let me go!

793
01:23:28,770 --> 01:23:29,978
Let go of me!

794
01:23:37,570 --> 01:23:39,446
- Hello?
- Where are you?

795
01:23:39,531 --> 01:23:40,572
I'm at the high school.

796
01:23:40,657 --> 01:23:42,366
Yeah, you need to get
out of there now.

797
01:23:42,450 --> 01:23:43,450
Why? What's happening?

798
01:23:43,535 --> 01:23:46,286
Your stunt with the car
is already on Youtube.

799
01:23:46,371 --> 01:23:47,811
If they're not right
on your ass now,

800
01:23:47,831 --> 01:23:49,540
- they will be soon.

801
01:23:50,124 --> 01:23:51,458
Come on.

802
01:23:51,543 --> 01:23:53,669
And don't tell me
this is not my fight.

803
01:23:53,753 --> 01:23:58,173
My dad probably knew those guys were
coming and that's why they took him.

804
01:23:58,842 --> 01:24:01,802
And also, I have your dog.

805
01:24:02,542 --> 01:24:03,863
- Look, I'm on my way.

806
01:24:03,888 --> 01:24:05,408
I'll meet you out
front of the school.

807
01:24:05,431 --> 01:24:07,266
- You've got to get out now.

808
01:24:07,892 --> 01:24:09,434
John?

809
01:24:09,519 --> 01:24:10,561
John!

810
01:24:15,233 --> 01:24:16,525
Let's go.

811
01:24:20,113 --> 01:24:23,323
-  Let go of me!

812
01:24:27,328 --> 01:24:29,830
- Jesus!

813
01:24:29,914 --> 01:24:33,667
Sarah! If you're in there, run!

814
01:24:33,751 --> 01:24:36,461
Run!

815
01:24:40,049 --> 01:24:42,968
Let me go!

816
01:24:48,850 --> 01:24:51,727
Listen to me. I'm not gonna
let them hurt you, Ok?

817
01:24:51,811 --> 01:24:54,438
Do you understand me? Come on.

818
01:26:08,262 --> 01:26:11,223
It'd be a good idea, cowboy, if you
kept your heroics off the Internet.

819
01:26:13,601 --> 01:26:17,813
- Who are you?
- Number Six. Where's your protector?

820
01:26:17,897 --> 01:26:21,274
- Dead.
- Yeah. Mine, too.

821
01:26:21,359 --> 01:26:22,734
Mogs got her four months ago.

822
01:26:22,819 --> 01:26:25,362
- We've been tracking them down.
- Tracking them?

823
01:26:25,446 --> 01:26:27,656
Yeah. Lucky for you,
I saved your ass.

824
01:26:27,740 --> 01:26:29,950
You should be watching
your own ass.

825
01:26:30,034 --> 01:26:32,285
Mogs have all the exits covered.

826
01:26:32,370 --> 01:26:35,330
Looks like you're gonna
have to fight to get out.

827
01:26:35,415 --> 01:26:37,624
- Are you game?
- Yeah.

828
01:26:37,709 --> 01:26:40,085
There's a tunnel under the school
that leads to the stadium.

829
01:26:40,169 --> 01:26:42,879
Oh, you made friends.
How nice.

830
01:26:45,008 --> 01:26:46,258
Let's go.

831
01:26:47,552 --> 01:26:50,137
Got any other legacies
I should know about?

832
01:26:50,221 --> 01:26:51,763
Stay tuned.

833
01:27:23,963 --> 01:27:26,423
- Oh, shit.

834
01:27:33,890 --> 01:27:35,265
Oh, shit!

835
01:27:45,068 --> 01:27:46,860
Careful, they'll see us.

836
01:27:48,196 --> 01:27:50,072
And you're going to
need all your energy.

837
01:27:54,202 --> 01:27:57,162
- What was that?
- They're comin'.

838
01:27:57,246 --> 01:27:59,664
- Ah! Whoa, whoa, whoa!

839
01:27:59,749 --> 01:28:02,209
Whoa! Sam, what are you doing?

840
01:28:02,293 --> 01:28:03,627
Did you see what just
flew out of that truck?

841
01:28:03,711 --> 01:28:05,879
And your dog just shape-shifted
into one of them.

842
01:28:05,963 --> 01:28:09,091
I thought he was gonna eat me.
Here's your rock.

843
01:28:11,177 --> 01:28:15,097
Hi! I'm Sam. What's your name?

844
01:28:16,140 --> 01:28:17,307
Jane Doe.

845
01:28:17,391 --> 01:28:18,642
That's cool. It's cool.

846
01:28:18,726 --> 01:28:20,060
So, are you a number, too?

847
01:28:20,144 --> 01:28:23,105
- Who is this tool?
- Sam, focus.

848
01:28:23,189 --> 01:28:25,732
- What flew out of the truck?

849
01:28:29,862 --> 01:28:32,405
- Come on! Go, go!

850
01:28:32,490 --> 01:28:35,742
- Sam. Come on! Go!

851
01:28:40,039 --> 01:28:41,790
Come on! Come on!

852
01:28:44,919 --> 01:28:47,212
- Come on!

853
01:29:47,273 --> 01:29:48,356
Ahh!

854
01:29:56,032 --> 01:29:58,325
- Hit me.
- What?

855
01:29:58,409 --> 01:30:00,785
With your lumen. I
need to power-up.

856
01:30:03,039 --> 01:30:04,372
Hit me!

857
01:30:15,384 --> 01:30:17,177
Red Bull's for pussies.

858
01:30:19,555 --> 01:30:21,640
He killed Henri. I want him.

859
01:30:53,381 --> 01:30:56,424
- Ah!

860
01:30:58,261 --> 01:30:59,636
Four!

861
01:31:11,857 --> 01:31:13,942
You're good with your hands.

862
01:31:14,026 --> 01:31:15,986
- Thanks.
- No problem.

863
01:31:17,488 --> 01:31:21,783
- My dog, he, uh... he just...
- Yeah, he's a chimera.

864
01:31:21,867 --> 01:31:23,994
He came with you from Lorien.

865
01:31:24,078 --> 01:31:26,454
Someone had to look after you.

866
01:32:29,560 --> 01:32:31,644
You brought a gun?
Are you serious?

867
01:32:31,729 --> 01:32:34,105
- What? It might come in handy.
- This way.

868
01:32:44,867 --> 01:32:45,867
Go!

869
01:32:54,877 --> 01:32:56,797
- Take her back to the tunnel!
- Got it! Come on!

870
01:33:03,844 --> 01:33:06,054
- Holy...!
- Ahh!

871
01:33:10,684 --> 01:33:11,935
I play a lot of Xbox.

872
01:33:18,275 --> 01:33:19,275
Oh!

873
01:33:39,588 --> 01:33:41,714
Oh! Ahh!

874
01:34:51,577 --> 01:34:55,830
Number Four, I think you
have something I need. Hm?

875
01:34:57,458 --> 01:35:01,794
Oh, thank you for making
this so nice and easy.

876
01:35:01,879 --> 01:35:07,091
Think of how quickly we'll finish off
the rest of the planet. It's fantastic!

877
01:35:07,885 --> 01:35:10,470
Soon, I'll be done
with all of you.

878
01:35:10,554 --> 01:35:12,764
- Just relax.

879
01:35:14,225 --> 01:35:17,936
You can't stop what's coming.
You never could.

880
01:35:18,020 --> 01:35:20,063
You have...

881
01:35:20,147 --> 01:35:22,565
- ...no idea...

882
01:35:23,776 --> 01:35:25,235
What I'm capable of.

883
01:35:41,502 --> 01:35:42,752
Ah!

884
01:36:39,727 --> 01:36:40,893
John.

885
01:36:44,189 --> 01:36:45,857
Fireproof?

886
01:36:47,067 --> 01:36:49,402
I told you to stay tuned.

887
01:37:18,349 --> 01:37:20,433
All right, give me that.
Come on.

888
01:37:21,352 --> 01:37:22,518
Thank you.

889
01:37:53,592 --> 01:37:57,553
Oh. Well, that was disappointing.
So, not a tracking device?

890
01:37:57,638 --> 01:37:59,681
No, it was.

891
01:37:59,765 --> 01:38:02,141
- Did you feel that, too?
- Yeah.

892
01:38:02,226 --> 01:38:05,395
- We know where we need to go.
- Yeah, we can find the others.

893
01:38:11,652 --> 01:38:14,821
- Here.
- Thank you.

894
01:38:15,823 --> 01:38:17,657
I hope this doesn't
get you in trouble.

895
01:38:17,741 --> 01:38:22,203
Nah. Stuff goes missing
from evidence all the time.

896
01:38:22,287 --> 01:38:24,664
My dad won't even know.

897
01:38:24,748 --> 01:38:27,583
- You want to be heading west now.
- Why?

898
01:38:27,668 --> 01:38:30,128
Because I told my dad
you're going east.

899
01:38:38,095 --> 01:38:41,931
- Six, Sam's coming with us.
- What?

900
01:38:43,100 --> 01:38:44,809
- No way.
- He's one of us now.

901
01:38:44,893 --> 01:38:47,103
We need to find his father.

902
01:38:50,733 --> 01:38:54,110
You slow us down, I'll
shoot you myself.

903
01:38:54,194 --> 01:38:56,612
And I believe you.
Could we go now?

904
01:39:02,619 --> 01:39:04,746
You know, I wouldn't leave
if it wasn't, uh...

905
01:39:04,830 --> 01:39:07,582
- Safer.
- Yeah.

906
01:39:07,666 --> 01:39:09,208
I know.

907
01:39:10,461 --> 01:39:12,879
Really sorry about what
happened with Henri.

908
01:39:14,173 --> 01:39:15,923
Me, too.

909
01:39:19,303 --> 01:39:21,804
You know I'll find you again.

910
01:39:24,141 --> 01:39:27,101
Probably still be here.

911
01:39:28,312 --> 01:39:29,896
It's the people that
make the place.

912
01:39:30,689 --> 01:39:32,982
- Right?
- Yeah.

913
01:39:39,364 --> 01:39:43,201
Henri warned me that we
only fall for one person.

914
01:39:45,454 --> 01:39:46,871
Ever?

915
01:39:47,748 --> 01:39:49,165
Ever.

916
01:41:21,967 --> 01:41:24,844
This is the first town
I've left without Henri.

917
01:41:25,804 --> 01:41:29,265
But it's also the first one I
have a reason to come back to.

918
01:41:30,642 --> 01:41:34,103
Henri was right, we're
stronger together.

919
01:41:34,688 --> 01:41:37,273
So we will find the others.

920
01:41:39,526 --> 01:41:44,113
My planet is called Lorien,
but Earth is my home now.

921
01:41:45,198 --> 01:41:48,868
It's as good a place as
any in the universe.

922
01:41:48,952 --> 01:41:51,329
And that's how it's
going to stay.

